ution Party candidates consolidate protest votes, though a Democratic win remains a long shot.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Brad Little (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Idaho's governor race pits Republican incumbent Brad Little, seeking a third term, against Democratic nominee Terri Pickens, with an independent, a Libertarian, and a Constitution Party candidate also on the ballot. Little won his primary in May and enters the general with the advantages of incumbency in a state that leans Republican by roughly eighteen points.\n\nPolling has been sparse but consistently favors Little: a July survey showed him ahead by twenty-one points, and a September poll by ten, with many voters still undecided. All seven expert raters call the race Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets put Democratic chances at only two to three percent. Republicans also hold the fundraising lead in every statewide race. The main uncertainty is the size of the margin, not the outcome, as third-party candidates may siphon votes from both major contenders.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0111, "margin": -14.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0115, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0087, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0158, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0168, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0122, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.015, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0193, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0058, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0101, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0244, "margin": -14.0}]}